# core.autocrlf is true on the machine this was written on, so a checkout would hand
# staging/init-oracle.sh CRLF line endings - and a bash script with CRLF endings, bind-mounted
# into a Linux container, fails on the shebang with "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M". The Oracle
# container would report a failed init script and the application would then fail every refresh
# against tables nobody created. LF is not a preference here; it is the file working.
*.sh text eol=lf
